{
  "_id": {
    "$oid": "68e81b4d967c07aa126814f0"
  },
  "name": "Patrick's Parabox",
  "genre": "[\"Strategy\",\"Casual\",\"Indie\",\"Puzzle\"]",
  "tags": "[\"Singleplayer\",\"Steam Achievements\",\"Full controller support\",\"Steam Cloud\",\"2D\",\"Horror\",\"Difficult\",\"Minimalist\",\"Abstract\",\"Logic\",\"Sokoban\"]",
  "publisher": "Patrick Traynor",
  "description": "Patrick's Parabox is an award-winning puzzle game that explores a unique recursive system of boxes within boxes within boxes within boxes. Learn to manipulate the world's structure by pushing boxes into and out of each other. Wrap your head around what happens when a box contains itself, and learn to use infinity to your advantage. Explore many more mechanics and recursive twists as you delve deeper and deeper into the system. It's boxes all the way down. The game has over 350 hand-crafted puzzles, which are designed to make you think, but also to guide you and showcase the beauty of the system. Each puzzle contains a new idea; there is no filler. A soothing, inquisitive soundtrack and sound design by Priscilla Snow mirrors new mechanics as they are introduced. (Note: the June 2021 demo includes this new music and sound!) Patrick's Parabox won the Excellence in Design award in the Independent Games Festival 2020. The game was also an IndieCade 2019 festival selection and received the IndieCade Developers Choice award.Show less",
  "url": "https://rawg.io/games/patricks-parabox",
  "image": "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/737/737028350ce7f1b2e555f3f757ff01dc.jpg",
