{
  "_id": {
    "$oid": "68e81b4d967c07aa126815cb"
  },
  "name": "Call of Juarez: Gunslinger",
  "genre": "[\"Action\",\"Shooter\"]",
  "tags": "[\"Singleplayer\",\"Steam Achievements\",\"Full controller support\",\"Steam Cloud\",\"Atmospheric\",\"steam-trading-cards\",\"Great Soundtrack\",\"Story Rich\",\"First-Person\",\"FPS\",\"Funny\",\"Gore\",\"Steam Leaderboards\",\"Comedy\",\"Historical\",\"Linear\",\"Narration\",\"Alternate History\",\"Western\",\"Bullet Time\",\"Dynamic Narration\"]",
  "publisher": "Ubisoft Entertainment",
  "description": "Gunslinger is the fourth installment of the Call of Juarez series of western-inspired games. The frame story, told in cutscenes, begins in 1910, in Kansas, where Silas, a patron in the pub, brags about his adventures in the Wild West. This old man claims he used to be a bounty hunter who took down many of the famous outlaws. Most of the game has the player re-enacting Silas's presumed past, while in the present the hero is narrating his own story off-screen. Silas is an unreliable narrator, however, and his own in-game audience will point at plot holes in his tall tales. Like the rest of Cal… Read more",
  "url": "https://rawg.io/games/call-of-juarez-gunslinger",
  "image": "https://media.rawg.io/media/games/a86/a86ce0afaf2d5ec2b0f048989f01795e.jpg",
