  "name": "F.E.A.R.",
  "genre": "[\"Action\",\"Shooter\"]",
  "tags": "[\"Singleplayer\",\"Multiplayer\",\"Atmospheric\",\"Great Soundtrack\",\"Story Rich\",\"First-Person\",\"Sci-fi\",\"Horror\",\"FPS\",\"Gore\",\"Classic\",\"Dark\",\"Survival Horror\",\"Masterpiece\",\"Bullet Time\"]",
  "publisher": "Warner Bros. Interactive",
  "description": "Following the plot of the game, you play as a Point Man, who works for F. E. A. R. - a fictional special forces unit, which is forced to resist the rebel squad of cloned supersoldiers. He also faces a supernatural threat - Alma, a ghostly creature in the form of a little girl. The game consists of 11 episodes with an epilogue. As for the plot, it is completely confused until the end. One of the primary abilities of the player is to slow down time. Being in this state for not so long, you can see the traces of flying bullets, move faster and get an advantage in battle. The whole game comes from the… Read more",
