  "tags": "[\"Singleplayer\",\"Steam Achievements\",\"Multiplayer\",\"Great Soundtrack\",\"Online multiplayer\",\"Split Screen\",\"Tactical\",\"Local Multiplayer\",\"War\",\"Turn-Based\",\"Historical\",\"Turn-Based Strategy\",\"Music\",\"World War II\",\"Turn-Based Tactics\",\"Card Game\",\"Soundtrack\",\"Mouse only\",\"Wargame\"]",
  "publisher": "HexWar Games",
  "description": "This 1 on 1 card game recreates the drama of the day Allied soldiers went ashore in occupied France, 6 June 1944. Each of the historic landing beaches - Sword, Juno, Gold, Omaha and Utah - is represented by its own card, as are the defending German divisions and attacking Allied units. The Allies must marshal their resources to gain and secure control of as many beaches as they can by day's end: a run-through of the 110-card deck. However, the Axis has the starting advantage; the Allies need to avoid being caught dead in the water. Although most units are preassigned to a beach, ea… Read more",
