  "name": "The Last Night",
  "genre": "[\"Action\",\"Adventure\",\"Strategy\",\"Simulation\",\"Indie\",\"Platformer\"]",
  "tags": "[\"Singleplayer\",\"Full controller support\",\"Atmospheric\",\"Story Rich\",\"2D\",\"Horror\",\"Violent\",\"Action-Adventure\",\"Pixel Graphics\",\"Point & Click\",\"Nudity\",\"Survival Horror\",\"Choices Matter\",\"3D\",\"Cinematic\",\"Cyberpunk\",\"Choose Your Own Adventure\",\"1980s\",\"Family Sharing\",\"Immersive Sim\"]",
  "publisher": "Raw Fury",
  "description": "Humans first knew the era of survival. Then they knew the era of work. Now they live in the era of leisure. Machines have surpassed human labour not only in strength, but in precision, intellect, and creativity. The fight for survival doesn’t mean food and water, but a purpose for living. People now define themselves by what they consume, not what they create. The Last Night immerses you in the everyday life of Charlie, a second-class citizen living in a city brimming with augmentation and citizens living a gamified existence -- none of which Charlie can experience himself du… Read more",
